    "text": "Brigantia is a goddess of the continental peoples and Britain. The northern part of the island held the Brigantes, a Brythonic folk, in early historical days. They venerated her as an ancestral deity. Her name lives on in the rivers Braint in Anglesey and Brent in Middlesex. Roman-era images and inscriptions join her with Victoria and Caelestis, the Syrian sky goddess. Her title translates as the high one. Some link her to the Irish Brigit. Scholars also tie her to the Gaulish goddess Brigindo.",
